+## Canva
+
+<!-- TO MEASURE: replace this with what a sign-in run against a real app showed, as the sections around it do. -->
+
+The operator's setup is in [`docs/old/canva-setup.md`](../old/canva-setup.md).
+
+- Canva's MCP server is `https://api.canva.com/connect/v1/mcp`. Its metadata
+  names `https://www.canva.com` as the authorization server, which offers PKCE
+  S256 and no registration, so each server's operator creates an app in the
+  Developer Portal and saves it under Connector apps, or names it in
+  `CANVA_CLIENT_CONFIG_PATH`.
+- Sign-ins come back to Switch Console on a listed loopback port.
+- The metadata lists no token endpoint authentication methods, which RFC 8414
+  reads as HTTP Basic.
+- It advertises no revocation endpoint, so the entry names one.
+- Asked for: `design:meta:read` and `design:content:read`, with
+  `design:content:write` for the write level. Not asked for: `folder:write`,
+  `brandtemplate:content:write`, `comment:write`, `asset:write` and
+  `help:answers:write`.
+
+To connect: Settings, Connections in Switch Console, then Canva. To roll back,
+add `canva` to `DISABLED_SERVICES`, remove its client under Connector apps or
+unset `CANVA_CLIENT_CONFIG_PATH`, or set the entry's `enabled: false`.
+
