+# Canva on a self-hosted server
+
+<!-- TO MEASURE: check each step against the Developer Portal while creating a real app. -->
+
+Agents can search, read and edit designs in their owners' Canva accounts once
+the server's operator creates a Canva app. Each person then connects their own
+Canva account from Switch Console and turns Canva on for the agents they choose.
+How it works is in
+[`docs/design/service-connections-v2.md`](../design/service-connections-v2.md),
+under Canva.
+
+Without the app, Canva is listed on the server as not set up.
+
+## Create the app
+
+In Canva's **Developer Portal**, create an app and turn on **Canva MCP** for it.
+
+1. **Scopes:** turn on `design:meta:read`, `design:content:read` and
+   `design:content:write`. Leave the rest off.
+2. **Redirect URLs:** add each of these, exactly. Sign-ins come back to Switch
+   Console on the person's own computer, and Canva matches the port too.
+   ```
+   http://127.0.0.1:39231/switch-services/callback
+   http://127.0.0.1:39232/switch-services/callback
+   http://127.0.0.1:39233/switch-services/callback
+   http://127.0.0.1:39234/switch-services/callback
+   http://127.0.0.1:39235/switch-services/callback
+   ```
+3. Copy the **client ID**, and generate a **client secret**.
+
+## Give it to Switch
+
+Save it under **Connector apps** in the dashboard, or name a file in
+`CANVA_CLIENT_CONFIG_PATH`, readable by the server and nobody else:
+
+```json
+{ "client_id": "<client id>", "client_secret": "<client secret>" }
+```
+
+## Switch it off
+
+Add `canva` to `DISABLED_SERVICES`, then remove the app under Connector apps or
+unset `CANVA_CLIENT_CONFIG_PATH`.
